1
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,180
Eighteen fifty-nine.

2
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,880
A man writes one quiet line:

3
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:20,940
Very probably.

4
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:34,920
Riemann drew a line across the dark

5
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:40,160
Every zero falling on one-half

6
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:44,820
A hundred sixty years of chalk and ash

7
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:50,560
Everyone could see it, no one made it last

8
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:54,800
Out in finite fields the story's told

9
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:59,980
Weil found the answer, Stepanov the road

10
00:01:00,170 --> 00:01:03,640
Build a function, make it vanish at each point

11
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:10,760
Stack the multiplicity till the zeros have nowhere to go

12
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:13,920
But the integers won't give you that

13
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:16,440
No Frobenius, no way back

14
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:20,080
If the world won't hand you multiplicity

15
00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:21,900
Build it

16
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:25,160
Lift it, lift it, theta after theta

17
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:30,400
Square root of X in a chain of light

18
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:35,700
Unitary to unitary, higher and higher

19
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:37,640
Every zero coming home tonight

20
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:43,880
To the line, to the line, to the line at one-half

21
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:51,860
Rallis on a seesaw, both sides balance even

22
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:57,720
The period turns Bessel, the characters fall away

23
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:02,080
Iwasawa towers climbing floor by floor

24
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:07,380
Like a finite field that keeps on opening doors

25
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:11,700
Primes and zeros settle up in the explicit formula

26
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:16,960
A positive sign where the variance falls

27
00:02:17,010 --> 00:02:21,920
No more Gauss sums, just Parseval k times

28
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:27,780
Square-root cancellation, honest as it climbs

29
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:30,080
Every lift has a price to pay

30
00:02:30,130 --> 00:02:32,940
Two-thirds of the way, it wants to stay

31
00:02:32,990 --> 00:02:35,640
Twist away the last stubborn ghost

32
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:38,760
Vandiver's shadow, where the K-groups hold

33
00:02:38,810 --> 00:02:41,980
Lift it, lift it, theta after theta

34
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:47,060
Square root of X in a chain of light

35
00:02:47,650 --> 00:02:52,460
Unitary to unitary, higher and higher

36
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:54,460
Every zero coming home tonight

37
00:02:54,510 --> 00:03:00,680
To the line, to the line, to the line at one-half

38
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:05,440
Seventeen million lines of Lean

39
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:10,820
Scanned for sorry, and found none

40
00:03:11,370 --> 00:03:16,280
No new axioms, but the build's not done

41
00:03:16,450 --> 00:03:21,520
Levent and Claude hand it to the kernel

42
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:27,400
When the build is done and the axioms are read

43
00:03:27,450 --> 00:03:32,840
Only three names left, nothing else instead

44
00:03:33,510 --> 00:03:36,460
Then the line is drawn

45
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:41,180
The line at one-half

46
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:44,200
The line at one-half

